{"title":"SFMT","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Theorem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Theorem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Proof\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Example_Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Example Problems</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Name\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Name</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Theorem\">Theorem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=SFMT&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Theorem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given nonnegative real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/9/ca901f3afacd576966bd661d7187b6ebaeaa67dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e_1, e_2, e_3, \\cdots ,e_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"13\" /> and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/4/1b4cee3dff8fffc3a4357356b5a71ae375475578.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1+x_2+x_3+\\cdots+x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"182\" height=\"13\" /> is fixed and all the terms inside the sum are nonnegative, the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/e/9feb59ade1a30333fa4ffa24dc7241dec9db5cb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1^{e_1}x_2^{e_2}x_3^{e_3}\\cdots x_n^{e_n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"19\" /> is when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/b/c3b793c1041b8f695c50809a9ccd2ca8eaa3aa9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{x_1}{e_1}=\\dfrac{x_2}{e_2}=\\dfrac{x_3}{e_3}=\\cdots =\\dfrac{x_n}{e_n}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"214\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=SFMT&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The weighted AM-GM Inequality states that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/b/ecbe2a675e27af0c6111e82c2c8667704a7f1ba3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\dotsc, a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"100\" height=\"11\" /> are nonnegative real numbers, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/6/04681e702e3cea71b0861891505d4b9e9a0ed0a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda_1, \\lambda_2, \\dotsc, \\lambda_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"103\" height=\"16\" /> are nonnegative real numbers (the \"weights\") which sum to 1, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/f/5ef0ac2abb71c15b0fee03768014fca7dbc39f37.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lambda_1 a_1 + \\lambda_2 a_2 + \\dotsb + \\lambda_n a_n \\ge a_1^{\\lambda_1} a_2^{\\lambda_2} \\dotsm a_n^{\\lambda_n}.\\]\" width=\"327\" height=\"20\" /> We let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/7/00753091697109c898b95311cb41fd807d0127fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda_i=\\dfrac{e_i}{e_1+e_2+\\cdots+e_n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"183\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/a/ebad9b68400090fc13818ba7ea9addc27be0a707.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i=\\dfrac{x_i}{e_i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"61\" height=\"37\" /> in this inequality. We get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/c/d5ce8d313f314e352697b422e11ea3697ffe98cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1+x_2+x_3+\\cdots+x_n \\ge \\sqrt[n]{\\dfrac{x_1^{e_1}x_2^{e_2}x_3^{e_3}\\cdots x_n^{e_n}}{e_1^{e_1}e_2^{e_2}e_3^{e_3}\\cdots e_n^{e_n}}}(e_1+e_2+e_3+\\cdots+e_n).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"553\" height=\"56\" /> Dividing both sides and then taking to the nth power, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/10989df94b8ac97751b71d8e4b9fbf0b2d8ca769.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\dfrac{x_1+x_2+x_3+\\cdots+x_n}{e_1+e_2+e_3+\\cdots+e_n}\\right)^n \\ge \\dfrac{x_1^{e_1}x_2^{e_2}x_3^{e_3}\\cdots x_n^{e_n}}{e_1^{e_1}e_2^{e_2}e_3^{e_3}\\cdots e_n^{e_n}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"382\" height=\"46\" />Then we can multiply both sides to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/b/b7b9a38f7eb578309365754ef44e047e88f2f905.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1^{e_1}x_2^{e_2}x_3^{e_3}\\cdots x_n^{e_n} \\le \\left(\\dfrac{x_1+x_2+x_3+\\cdots+x_n}{e_1+e_2+e_3+\\cdots+e_n}\\right)^n (e_1^{e_1}e_2^{e_2}e_3^{e_3}\\cdots e_n^{e_n}).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"513\" height=\"46\" /> The equality case for the weighted AM-GM inequality is when all the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> terms such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/a/26ae315076f64895667486f0c8faaa5ea17b5d59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are equal, or in this case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/a/d6a98b7090078effbb9a60f525e0b344d4349620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{x_1}{e_1}=\\dfrac{x_2}{e_2}=\\dfrac{x_3}{e_3}=\\cdots=\\dfrac{x_n}{e_n}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"214\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Example_Problems\">Example Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=SFMT&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Example Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=SFMT&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Given nonnegative integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/0/d20258310be3455daf8318274224a9d1d28fb6a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y, z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"11\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/f/83f52bdec6fd6bb08ce00f17d7da85d4c28ea57f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=16,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"17\" /> find the maximum value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/d/93d5dad2631d257bce1fc1355454a1ade452301f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3y^2z^3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=SFMT&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>By the new theorem, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/7/6b7e56302301a46b7967821851db9552d8a43557.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{x}{3}=\\dfrac{y}{2}=\\dfrac{z}{3},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"34\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/5/c3527f0d9812b93d84beda782df8367f5bf5c195.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=6, y=4, z=6.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"152\" height=\"17\" /> Plugging it in, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/b/37b7c41a048b5fb02e357b8a333d75ca25a6c2de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$746496.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Name\">Name</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=SFMT&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Name\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This theorem has been widely known for a while now. The AoPS user solasky rediscovered it and put a name to it. You can call it whatever you want.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018105728\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.014 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.027 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 127/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4805/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:22046:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018105728 and revision id 162799. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}